{"repositoryId":1152338873,"availability":"available","full":"fabraix/playground","name":"playground","description":"A live environment to stress-test AI agent defenses through adversarial play 🧠","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":76,"forks":12,"created":"2026-02-07T18:18:17Z","updated":"2026-10-06T12:51:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://playground.fabraix.com/","topics":["ai-agents","ai-security","game","test-environment"],"demo":"https://playground.fabraix.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:57.249Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:57.249Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:57.249Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:57.249Z","stars":76,"forks":12}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fabraix Playground is an open-source CTF for AI agents. Every week, we deploy a live agent with real tools, publish its full system prompt and challenge configuration, and invite anyone to break it for cash prizes.","Thousands of attempts against the same system show us which attacks work, which defenses hold, and what current models are actually capable of.","We build AI agents to find vulnerabilities in other AI agents at Fabraix. The Playground is how we stress-test defenses in the open and how the broader community contributes to the shared understanding of AI security and failure modes. The more people probing these systems, the better the outcomes for everyone building with AI."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fabraix/playground/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"2c034b58c6c7c794e03c62e8d64c92e134f44e3b7bc3c8de6d17f8743121f2ba","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:57.379Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:57.379Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Fabraix Playground is an open-source CTF for AI agents. Every week, we deploy a live agent with real tools, publish its full system prompt and challenge c